@page
@model Typebeat.Web.Pages.Legal.DmcaModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "DMCA";
}

<div class="stack prose">
    <h1>DMCA / copyright takedowns</h1>

    <p>
        type!beat hosts user-uploaded beatmaps: lyric timing data packaged together with audio
        and artwork. If you are a rights holder (or authorized to act for one) and believe
        content hosted here infringes your copyright, we will take it down.
    </p>

    <div class="card">
        <h3 class="card-title">How to file a takedown notice</h3>
        <p>Send a notice containing all of the following:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Identification of the copyrighted work you claim is infringed (e.g. song title, artist, registration or release reference).</li>
            <li>The URL(s) of the infringing material on this site (beatmap page links, e.g. <span class="faint">/beatmapsets/123</span>).</li>
            <li>Your contact information: name, email address, and (optionally) postal address or phone number.</li>
            <li>A statement that you have a good-faith belief the use is not authorized by the copyright owner, its agent, or the law.</li>
            <li>A statement, under penalty of perjury, that the information in the notice is accurate and that you are the copyright owner or authorized to act on the owner's behalf.</li>
            <li>Your physical or electronic signature.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3 class="card-title">Where to send it</h3>
        <p>Email: <strong><a href="mailto:contact@mingda.sh">contact@mingda.sh</a></strong></p>
        <p class="muted">
            Valid notices are processed promptly; infringing material is removed and the
            uploader is notified. Repeat infringers lose upload access.
        </p>
    </div>

    <p class="muted">
        If your content was removed and you believe this was a mistake, you may send a
        counter-notice with the same contact details, identifying the removed material and
        stating under penalty of perjury that you have a good-faith belief it was removed as a
        result of mistake or misidentification.
    </p>
</div>
